<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=5.0" />
  <title>{pageTitle}</title>
  <meta name="description" content={pageDescription} />
  <meta name="keywords" content="dearness allowance explanation, aicpi iw index da formula, da tracker central government, dearness relief for pensioners, da on transport allowance, 8th pay commission da reset to zero" />
  <meta name="robots" content="index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large" />
  <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />

  <!-- Open Graph -->
  <meta property="og:locale" content="en_IN" />
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:title" content={pageTitle} />
  <meta property="og:description" content={pageDescription} />
  <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalURL} />
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="8th Pay Commission Portal" />

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />

  <!-- Schema.org WebPage + FAQPage -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "WebPage",
        "name": pageTitle,
        "url": canonicalURL.toString(),
        "description": pageDescription,
        "inLanguage": "en-IN"
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": faqs.map((f) => ({
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": f.q,
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a }
        }))
      }
    ]
  })} />

  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #f8fafc;
      --surface: #ffffff;
      --surface-subtle: #f1f5f9;
      --border: #e2e8f0;
      --primary: #1d4ed8;
      --primary-hover: #1e40af;
      --primary-gradient: linear-gradient(135deg, #1d4ed8 0%, #0284c7 100%);
      --text: #0f172a;
      --text-muted: #64748b;
      --accent-green: #15803d;
      --accent-green-bg: #dcfce7;
      --radius-sm: 8px;
      --radius-md: 14px;
      --radius-lg: 20px;
      --shadow-sm: 0 1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
      --shadow-md: 0 4px 12px -2px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
      --shadow-lg: 0 16px 32px -4px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; }
    body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 15px; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
    a { color: var(--primary); text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.2s ease; }
    a:hover { color: var(--primary-hover); }

    .layout-wrap { max-width: 1160px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.25rem; }

    /* Hero Header */
    .hero-header {
      text-align: center;
      padding: 3rem 1rem 1.75rem;
    }
    .badge-pill {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.4rem;
      background: #eff6ff;
      border: 1px solid #bfdbfe;
      color: #1d4ed8;
      padding: 0.25rem 0.85rem;
      border-radius: 30px;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    }
    .hero-header h1 {
      font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: -0.035em;
      line-height: 1.22;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .hero-header p {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      max-width: 780px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    /* Calculator Main Box */
    .calc-box {
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
      padding: 2rem;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    }
    .chip-bar {
      display: flex;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      overflow-x: auto;
      padding: 0.5rem 0 1.25rem;
      scrollbar-width: none;
    }
    .chip-bar::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
    .chip-btn {
      background: #f1f5f9;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      color: #475569;
      padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem;
      border-radius: 30px;
      font-size: 0.84rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      white-space: nowrap;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: all 0.15s ease;
    }
    .chip-btn:hover { background: #e2e8f0; }
    .chip-btn.active {
      background: var(--primary);
      border-color: var(--primary);
      color: #ffffff;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(29, 78, 216, 0.3);
    }

    .form-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
      gap: 1.25rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .form-item {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }
    .form-item label {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #334155;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    }
    .form-item input, .form-item select {
      background: #ffffff;
      border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1;
      color: var(--text);
      padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      outline: none;
      transition: all 0.2s;
    }
    .form-item input:focus, .form-item select:focus {
      border-color: var(--primary);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.15);
    }

    /* Live Summary Cards */
    .summary-cards {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .kpi-unit {
      background: #f8fafc;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
      padding: 1.25rem;
      text-align: center;
      position: relative;
    }
    .kpi-unit.highlight {
      background: #eff6ff;
      border-color: #bfdbfe;
    }
    .kpi-unit.success {
      background: var(--accent-green-bg);
      border-color: #86efac;
    }
    .kpi-unit .kpi-label {
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }
    .kpi-unit .kpi-val {
      font-size: 1.45rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .kpi-unit.highlight .kpi-val { color: var(--primary); }
    .kpi-unit.success .kpi-val { color: var(--accent-green); }

    /* Breakdown Box */
    .breakdown-box {
      background: #f8fafc;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }
    .breakdown-title {
      font-weight: 800;
      font-size: 1rem;
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .breakdown-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-size: 0.94rem;
    }
    .breakdown-table td {
      padding: 0.65rem 0.5rem;
      border-bottom: 1px dashed #cbd5e1;
    }
    .breakdown-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
    .breakdown-table td.num {
      text-align: right;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    /* Content Area */
    .article-wrap {
      background: var(--surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
      padding: 2.75rem;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    }
    .article-wrap h2 {
      font-size: 1.6rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: var(--text);
      letter-spacing: -0.025em;
      margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
      padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
      border-bottom: 2px solid #eff6ff;
    }
    .article-wrap h3 {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #1e293b;
      margin: 1.6rem 0 0.65rem;
    }
    .article-wrap p {
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
      color: #334155;
      font-size: 1.02rem;
    }
    .article-wrap ul, .article-wrap ol {
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      color: #334155;
    }
    .article-wrap li { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }

    .formula-banner {
      background: #eff6ff;
      border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);
      padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem;
      border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      font-family: monospace;
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      color: #1e40af;
    }

    /* Tables */
    .table-responsive {
      overflow-x: auto;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }
    table.data-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 0.91rem;
    }
    table.data-table th, table.data-table td {
      padding: 0.8rem 0.95rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    table.data-table th {
      background: #f8fafc;
      color: #475569;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    table.data-table tr:hover td { background: #f8fafc; }

    /* FAQ */
    .faq-unit {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 1.15rem 0;
    }
    .faq-quest {
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--text);
      cursor: pointer;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      font-size: 1.02rem;
    }
    .faq-ans {
      display: none;
      padding-top: 0.65rem;
      color: #475569;
      font-size: 0.96rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .faq-unit.open .faq-ans { display: block; }
    .faq-unit.open .faq-arrow { transform: rotate(180deg); }
    .faq-arrow { transition: transform 0.2s ease; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-muted); }

    /* Mobile Sticky Bar */
    .mobile-sticky-bar {
      display: none;
      position: fixed;
      bottom: 0;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
      z-index: 990;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      box-shadow: 0 -4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
    }
    .mobile-sticky-bar .lbl { font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700; }
    .mobile-sticky-bar .val { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--primary); }
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .mobile-sticky-bar { display: flex; }
      body { padding-bottom: 4.5rem; }
    }

    /* Disclaimer */
    .disclaimer-strip {
      max-width: 1160px;
      margin: 2rem auto 4rem;
      padding: 1.25rem;
      background: #f8fafc;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-left: 4px solid #94a3b8;
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: #64748b;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <main class="layout-wrap">

    <!-- HERO HEADER -->
    <header class="hero-header">
      <div class="badge-pill">Cost of Living & AICPI-IW Index Analysis</div>
      <h1>Dearness Allowance (DA) & AICPI Tracker</h1>
      <p>Comprehensive guide to Central Government Dearness Allowance (DA) and Dearness Relief (DR): understand the 12-month AICPI-IW formula, track semi-annual revisions, and calculate monthly payouts.</p>
    </header>

    <!-- INTERACTIVE DA & AICPI CALCULATOR WIDGET -->
    <section class="calc-box" aria-label="Dearness Allowance Interactive Calculation Widget">
      
      <!-- Quick Rate Selection Chips -->
      <div style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        <span style="font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; color: #64748b; text-transform: uppercase;">Simulate or Select DA Percentage Rate:</span>
        <div class="chip-bar" id="daRatePills">
          <button class="chip-btn" data-da="0">0% (8th CPC Reset Base)</button>
          <button class="chip-btn" data-da="4">4% (Projected 1st Installment)</button>
          <button class="chip-btn" data-da="25">25% (HRA Trigger 1)</button>
          <button class="chip-btn" data-da="50">50% (HRA Trigger 2)</button>
          <button class="chip-btn active" data-da="53">53% (Current 7th CPC Status)</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Controls Grid -->
      <div class="form-grid">
        <div class="form-item">
          <label for="daLevelPreset">Pay Matrix Level (Preset)</label>
          <select id="daLevelPreset">
            {daMatrixTiers.map((item) => (
              <option value={item.basePay} selected={item.level.startsWith("Level 6")}>
                {item.level} - Base Pay: ₹{item.basePay.toLocaleString('en-IN')}
              </option>
            ))}
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="form-item">
          <label for="daBasicInput">Current Monthly Basic Pay (₹)</label>
          <input type="number" id="daBasicInput" value="35400" min="18000" step="100" />
        </div>

        <div class="form-item">
          <label for="daPercentInput">Dearness Allowance Rate (%)</label>
          <input type="number" id="daPercentInput" value="53" min="0" max="150" step="1" />
        </div>

        <div class="form-item">
          <label for="daTransportSelect">Transport Allowance (TA) Tier</label>
          <select id="daTransportSelect">
            <option value="3600" selected>Higher TPTA Metro - Level 3 to 8 (₹3,600 Base)</option>
            <option value="7200">Higher TPTA Metro - Level 9 & Above (₹7,200 Base)</option>
            <option value="1800">Other Locations - Level 3 to 8 (₹1,800 Base)</option>
            <option value="3600">Other Locations - Level 9 & Above (₹3,600 Base)</option>
            <option value="1350">Level 1 & 2 Base TPTA (₹1,350 Base)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Live Summary KPI Cards -->
      <div class="summary-cards">
        <div class="kpi-unit">
          <div class="kpi-label">Monthly DA on Basic Pay</div>
          <div class="kpi-val" id="dispDaBasic">₹18,762</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-unit highlight">
          <div class="kpi-label">Monthly DA on Transport (TA)</div>
          <div class="kpi-val" id="dispDaTa">₹1,908</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-unit success">
          <div class="kpi-label">Total Monthly DA Disbursal</div>
          <div class="kpi-val" id="dispTotalDa">₹20,670</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed Arithmetic Slip -->
      <div class="breakdown-box">
        <div class="breakdown-title">
          <span>Monthly Dearness Allowance Disbursal Breakdown</span>
          <span style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 0.85rem;" id="slipLevelLabel">Level 6 (GP 4200) • 53% DA Rate</span>
        </div>
        <table class="breakdown-table">
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Current Monthly Basic Pay Entitlement</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipBasic">₹35,400</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Applicable Dearness Allowance Percentage</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipDaRate">53%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Monthly Dearness Allowance on Basic (Basic Pay × DA %)</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipBasicDa">₹18,762</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Base Transport Allowance (TA) Rate</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipBaseTa">₹3,600</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Dearness Allowance on Transport Allowance (Base TA × DA %)</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipTaDa">₹1,908</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="font-weight: 700; background: #f8fafc;">
              <td>Total Monthly Transport Allowance Disbursed (Base TA + DA on TA)</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipTotalTa" style="color: var(--primary);">₹5,508</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="font-weight: 800; background: var(--accent-green-bg);">
              <td style="color: var(--accent-green);">Net Monthly DA Disbursed Across Salary (Basic DA + TA DA)</td>
              <td class="num" id="slipNetDa" style="color: var(--accent-green);">₹20,670</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- IN-DEPTH 1,300+ WORDS FRESH SEO ARTICLE -->
    <article class="article-wrap">
      <h2>1. The Economic Rationale: What is Dearness Allowance?</h2>
      <p>
        In public finance, salaries and pensions cannot remain static against inflation. Because basic pay scales under Central Pay Commissions remain fixed for a decade at a time, retail price surges would steadily erode the real living standards of civil servants and armed forces veterans. 
      </p>
      <p>
        To prevent this loss of purchasing power, the Government of India provides a dedicated cost-of-living adjustment known as <strong>Dearness Allowance (DA)</strong>. For active employees across Central Ministries, Indian Railways, the Department of Posts, and Defence establishments, DA is added directly to monthly basic pay. For pensioners and family pensioners, the identical financial protection is disbursed as <strong>Dearness Relief (DR)</strong> on their basic pension.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The Official AICPI-IW Formula: How DA is Computed</h2>
      <p>
        Dearness Allowance is determined through an audited mathematical formula tied to the <strong>All-India Consumer Price Index for Industrial Workers (AICPI-IW)</strong>. The index is compiled and released monthly by the <strong>Labour Bureau</strong> under the Ministry of Labour & Employment.
      </p>
      <p>
        The 7th Central Pay Commission established the current computation formula, referencing the 12-month average of the AICPI-IW with base year 2001=100 (converted to the modern 2016=100 series via a linking factor of 2.88):
      </p>

      <div class="formula-banner">
        DA % = [((Average of AICPI-IW for the last 12 months − 261.42) ÷ 261.42) × 100]
      </div>

      <p>
        Where <strong>261.42</strong> represents the base index benchmark corresponding to January 1, 2016, the date the 7th CPC took effect.
      </p>

      <h3>The Statutory Truncation Rule</h3>
      <p>
        A key administrative rule enforced by the Department of Expenditure is the <strong>Truncation Rule</strong>. In DA computations, decimals are never rounded up, regardless of how close the value is to the next integer:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>If the formula yields <strong>53.89%</strong>, the approved DA increase is strictly <strong>53%</strong>.</li>
        <li>The remaining fractional index points (0.89%) are not lost; they carry forward into the 12-month moving average for the subsequent determination cycle.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Revision Frequency: The January and July Cycles</h2>
      <p>
        Dearness Allowance is revised semi-annually, following a consistent calendar rhythm:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>January 1st Revision:</strong> Calculated using the 12-month AICPI-IW index data from <em>January 1st to December 31st</em> of the preceding calendar year. The Union Cabinet typically approves this installment in March or April, disbursing it alongside retroactive arrears for January and February.</li>
        <li><strong>July 1st Revision:</strong> Calculated using the 12-month AICPI-IW index data from <em>July 1st of the previous year to June 30th</em> of the current year. This installment is traditionally announced in September or October ahead of major festive holidays, accompanied by arrears for July, August, and September.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Historical Progression: The 7th CPC DA Trajectory (0% to 53%+)</h2>
      <p>
        Reviewing the trajectory of Dearness Allowance across the 7th Pay Commission illustrates how retail inflation compounds over a decade:
      </p>

      <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Effective Date</th>
              <th>Notified DA Rate</th>
